1
00:00:05,727 --> 00:00:06,897
What's that sound?

2
00:00:11,107 --> 00:00:13,447
Wake up, both of you!
Snakes everywhere!

3
00:00:13,897 --> 00:00:15,197
What should we do?

4
00:00:15,697 --> 00:00:18,697
Ja'far, Mystras! Live on for me!

5
00:00:34,467 --> 00:00:37,177
Let's restore our energy by eating this!

6
00:00:37,797 --> 00:00:38,637
Ja'far...

7
00:00:39,217 --> 00:00:40,887
You're... going to eat that?

8
00:00:41,717 --> 00:00:45,267
I've strangled and eaten many of these
during my assassin years.

9
00:00:47,097 --> 00:00:48,937
Let's eat!

10
00:00:49,017 --> 00:00:49,937
Yes!

11
00:00:50,017 --> 00:00:53,357
Take your time, there's plenty of them!

12
00:01:00,697 --> 00:01:04,367
All right, I'm done butchering snakes
for tonight.

13
00:01:05,577 --> 00:01:08,747
Ja'far, are you making progress with that?

14
00:01:09,087 --> 00:01:09,917
Yeah.

15
00:01:10,457 --> 00:01:13,507
I've finished weaving this cloth
made from tree barks.

16
00:01:14,467 --> 00:01:16,377
Wow. I'm impressed, Ja'far.

17
00:01:17,217 --> 00:01:19,347
There's been so many squalls recently.

18
00:01:19,967 --> 00:01:21,927
Let's hope this prevents leakage.

19
00:01:22,387 --> 00:01:23,307
Hey, guys!

20
00:01:24,887 --> 00:01:25,937
Check this out.

21
00:01:26,347 --> 00:01:29,647
A sturdy branch washed ashore,
thanks to the rain the other day.

22
00:01:30,227 --> 00:01:32,317
Great! That's perfect building wood.

23
00:01:33,027 --> 00:01:35,527
All right! Let's repair the house
this afternoon.

24
00:01:36,277 --> 00:01:39,157
But let's have lunch first.
It's all ready to eat.

25
00:01:39,447 --> 00:01:40,317
-Yes!
-Yes!

26
00:01:45,247 --> 00:01:47,367
Yet another day of snake meat...

27
00:01:48,287 --> 00:01:50,667
I'm getting sick of this flavor.

28
00:01:51,997 --> 00:01:52,997
Ja'far.

29
00:01:53,747 --> 00:01:54,757
Here.

30
00:01:54,837 --> 00:01:56,797
Is this rock salt?!

31
00:01:56,877 --> 00:01:59,717
I found it exposed on the cliff behind.

32
00:01:59,797 --> 00:02:01,137
Way to go, Sin!

33
00:02:02,677 --> 00:02:04,137
This one's ready, too.

34
00:02:04,677 --> 00:02:06,227
Go for it, Mystras.

35
00:02:06,637 --> 00:02:09,647
Wow, that looks delicious!

36
00:02:11,227 --> 00:02:14,107
But... wait a minute!

37
00:02:14,647 --> 00:02:17,817
Why are we adapting to this lifestyle?!

38
00:02:18,397 --> 00:02:20,447
This is absurd!

39
00:02:20,947 --> 00:02:24,787
Don't you remember why we're here
in the first place?

40
00:02:25,617 --> 00:02:27,447
The reason why we're here?

41
00:02:28,997 --> 00:02:31,077
-That's right, to survive.
-That's right, to survive.

42
00:02:32,537 --> 00:02:36,337
You've got to be kidding me!

43
00:04:10,977 --> 00:04:13,017
This is the Artemyra Kingdom.

44
00:04:13,597 --> 00:04:17,857
We were tossed to the bottom of the valley
because we enraged the queen.

45
00:04:18,857 --> 00:04:22,147
Our goal was to establish diplomacy
with Artemyra.

46
00:04:22,487 --> 00:04:26,567
So, we must return alive
and face the queen again!

47
00:04:27,317 --> 00:04:29,737
I vaguely remember,
now that you've mentioned it.

48
00:04:29,827 --> 00:04:31,747
I remember, too.

49
00:04:31,827 --> 00:04:32,657
Then...!

50
00:04:33,707 --> 00:04:36,167
But I'm pretty comfortable
living here now.

51
00:04:37,127 --> 00:04:38,747
Oh, this one's ready, too.

52
00:04:39,037 --> 00:04:40,047
Thanks.

53
00:04:41,667 --> 00:04:44,797
It's surely a lot more pleasant
than my Sham Lash years.

54
00:04:44,877 --> 00:04:46,547
No!

55
00:04:47,757 --> 00:04:49,677
I realized something by living here.

56
00:04:50,757 --> 00:04:54,477
When I was young,
food was scarce because of the war.

57
00:04:55,437 --> 00:04:56,937
We all helped each other out,

58
00:04:57,517 --> 00:04:59,727
desperately trying to survive each day.

59
00:05:01,317 --> 00:05:04,647
But... I'd forgotten about those times.

60
00:05:05,147 --> 00:05:06,907
I ate excessively well in Reim.

61
00:05:07,817 --> 00:05:10,407
Sleeping in a warm bed
had become the norm.

62
00:05:10,947 --> 00:05:13,287
I was far from being poor.

63
00:05:14,617 --> 00:05:18,497
I've come to realize how I was living
a luxurious and blessed lifestyle.

64
00:05:19,337 --> 00:05:23,087
Living in the bottom of the valley
has humbled me quite a bit.

65
00:05:25,167 --> 00:05:27,797
I'm grateful for the blessings
of the sun and nature.

66
00:05:28,337 --> 00:05:32,057
I pay respects to the animals
who give us their lives.

67
00:05:33,267 --> 00:05:35,477
Yes, this...

68
00:05:36,187 --> 00:05:39,187
is truly what it means "to live."

69
00:05:42,607 --> 00:05:43,437
Sin...

70
00:05:44,937 --> 00:05:46,527
A complete waste of time.

71
00:05:47,777 --> 00:05:50,027
I didn't ask you for enlightenment!

72
00:05:50,987 --> 00:05:53,867
I just want to get out of here
as soon as possible.

73
00:05:54,787 --> 00:05:56,157
-Really?
-Really?

74
00:06:06,547 --> 00:06:10,427
It's hopeless.
They've forgotten about everything.

75
00:06:10,887 --> 00:06:13,557
Their only concern is how to adapt better.

76
00:06:14,637 --> 00:06:18,387
We're going to end up living
at the bottom of this valley forever.

77
00:06:19,057 --> 00:06:20,187
I won't let that happen.

78
00:06:20,977 --> 00:06:23,687
If I get out of here,
I can see that lady...

79
00:06:24,267 --> 00:06:26,397
If you return from the valley,

80
00:06:26,487 --> 00:06:28,647
let me show you a good time.

81
00:06:29,397 --> 00:06:30,737
No, not that.

82
00:06:31,157 --> 00:06:34,537
I want to fulfill my dream
of traveling the world with Sinbad!

83
00:06:35,237 --> 00:06:37,997
I have to get out of here, no matter what.

84
00:06:40,167 --> 00:06:41,077
Huh?

85
00:06:44,337 --> 00:06:45,417
Holy smokes!

86
00:06:46,627 --> 00:06:49,627
What is it? I want to go back to sleep.

87
00:06:50,217 --> 00:06:51,297
What?!

88
00:06:52,177 --> 00:06:53,597
-Fresh meat?!
-Fresh meat?!

89
00:06:54,347 --> 00:06:56,807
A little rotten,
but it's still mouth-watering meat!

90
00:06:57,677 --> 00:06:58,767
It's lamb, too!

91
00:06:59,227 --> 00:07:01,687
How did this get to the bottom
of the valley?!

92
00:07:01,767 --> 00:07:03,807
Mystras, how did you find this?

93
00:07:04,437 --> 00:07:08,397
I found it on the ground
while searching the area last night.

94
00:07:08,987 --> 00:07:12,067
It was already processed when I found it.

95
00:07:12,907 --> 00:07:15,367
So... that means...

96
00:07:18,077 --> 00:07:20,247
we'll have a lamb feast tonight!

97
00:07:20,327 --> 00:07:21,497
Woo-hoo!

98
00:07:21,577 --> 00:07:23,497
No!

99
00:07:24,327 --> 00:07:25,957
Think about it!

100
00:07:26,037 --> 00:07:29,467
This meat has clearly been processed
by human hands!

101
00:07:29,757 --> 00:07:31,837
Don't you think it's suspicious

102
00:07:31,927 --> 00:07:33,757
that it's here?!

103
00:07:33,837 --> 00:07:34,967
It's not a coincidence!

104
00:07:35,547 --> 00:07:37,677
Someone intentionally placed
the fresh meat here.

105
00:07:37,757 --> 00:07:40,267
It could be a clue to our escape!

106
00:07:40,847 --> 00:07:41,807
I want it rare.

107
00:07:42,057 --> 00:07:44,517
That's too risky. It has to be well-done.

108
00:07:47,267 --> 00:07:48,227
Huh?

109
00:07:49,777 --> 00:07:51,947
What's this rock doing here?

110
00:07:53,657 --> 00:07:54,817
It's a precious stone.

111
00:07:55,277 --> 00:07:58,237
You can find a lot of those here.

112
00:07:58,787 --> 00:08:01,287
But I've been ignoring them
since they're inedible.

113
00:08:02,117 --> 00:08:04,537
You're right. We can't even eat it.

114
00:08:04,627 --> 00:08:05,787
Precious stones...

115
00:08:06,707 --> 00:08:08,837
Even precious stones lost to hunger...

116
00:08:10,047 --> 00:08:13,797
These two are far too comfortable
to ever get out of here.

117
00:08:16,507 --> 00:08:17,677
Mystras.

118
00:08:18,347 --> 00:08:21,057
You've led us
into a game-changing situation.

119
00:08:22,057 --> 00:08:25,267
This may be the decisive blow

120
00:08:25,347 --> 00:08:27,307
that will break the deadlock.

121
00:08:28,477 --> 00:08:31,607
Now, show me where you found this meat.

122
00:08:33,107 --> 00:08:33,947
Yes.

123
00:08:48,247 --> 00:08:49,837
Unbelievable.

124
00:08:50,547 --> 00:08:52,707
They weren't here this afternoon.

125
00:08:52,797 --> 00:08:53,667
Yeah.

126
00:08:54,297 --> 00:08:57,217
I wonder who's responsible...

127
00:08:57,797 --> 00:08:58,757
and why.

128
00:09:10,147 --> 00:09:11,357
It's fine meat!

129
00:09:12,397 --> 00:09:13,777
-Gather them all!
-Yes!

130
00:09:14,147 --> 00:09:17,317
Will you quit gathering the meat
and listen for once?!

131
00:09:17,907 --> 00:09:20,657
Of course,
I'm very curious about this meat, too.

132
00:09:21,157 --> 00:09:23,287
But first, we gotta gather them all!

133
00:09:24,997 --> 00:09:25,827
Exactly!

134
00:09:26,247 --> 00:09:27,287
Balalark Meat!

135
00:09:27,827 --> 00:09:28,997
What the heck are you saying?!

136
00:09:30,377 --> 00:09:32,707
Finding out the truth comes first!

137
00:09:33,257 --> 00:09:36,837
This meat might give us a clue
on how to get out of here!

138
00:09:37,717 --> 00:09:39,047
Hey! Give that back!

139
00:09:39,137 --> 00:09:40,047
Don't you dare!

140
00:09:47,517 --> 00:09:49,687
It's those birds of Artemyra!

141
00:09:51,187 --> 00:09:52,357
They're over here, too!

142
00:09:52,437 --> 00:09:54,647
Darn it! That's our meat!

143
00:09:58,607 --> 00:10:02,277
The birds snatched all of them.

144
00:10:03,447 --> 00:10:04,617
No...

145
00:10:05,117 --> 00:10:07,787
That meat could've led us to a way out.

146
00:10:09,917 --> 00:10:10,957
Now it's hopeless.

147
00:10:14,497 --> 00:10:16,837
It's gonna be okay, Mystras.

148
00:10:17,837 --> 00:10:20,177
We've survived up until now.

149
00:10:21,137 --> 00:10:23,927
It seems like fate is on our side.

150
00:10:30,897 --> 00:10:32,107
That's strange.

151
00:10:32,607 --> 00:10:36,397
They're gathering far less stones
than before.

152
00:10:36,647 --> 00:10:39,317
It's the birdies' fault.

153
00:10:39,397 --> 00:10:43,527
So true. They haven't brought us
any meat recently.

154
00:10:43,617 --> 00:10:44,737
No excuses!

155
00:10:45,327 --> 00:10:48,827
But we're trying our best.

156
00:10:48,907 --> 00:10:51,167
So true! You're being tyrannical.

157
00:10:51,247 --> 00:10:53,877
Silence!
Your pay will be commission-based!

158
00:10:54,127 --> 00:10:57,587
So, it will decrease if you can't gather
a sufficient amount!

159
00:10:57,667 --> 00:10:58,797
Oh, no!

160
00:10:58,877 --> 00:11:01,507
If I can't make any money,
my wife will kill me!

161
00:11:01,757 --> 00:11:04,677
Same here, my lady!

162
00:11:05,257 --> 00:11:09,267
Okay, fine! Just focus and keep working!

163
00:11:09,557 --> 00:11:11,347
We'll figure something out on our end.

164
00:11:11,437 --> 00:11:15,897
My lady, you're truly womanly and great!

165
00:11:15,977 --> 00:11:18,647
Women are so reliable!

166
00:11:20,567 --> 00:11:21,657
Hurry!

167
00:11:21,737 --> 00:11:25,527
We gotta gather them all
before the birds take them away again.

168
00:11:26,117 --> 00:11:28,997
Don't leave anything! Let's do this!

169
00:11:30,867 --> 00:11:33,627
He said, "Fate was on our side."

170
00:11:34,167 --> 00:11:37,417
He just wants to eat the meat after all.

171
00:11:38,337 --> 00:11:40,167
I can't trust anyone anymore.

172
00:11:41,927 --> 00:11:44,297
I'm gonna be stuck here forever.

173
00:11:45,137 --> 00:11:47,137
Do not worry, Mystras.

174
00:11:48,767 --> 00:11:50,637
Sin has a plan.

175
00:11:51,887 --> 00:11:54,477
He's the type of man who can...

176
00:11:54,977 --> 00:11:58,107
turn futility into an act of destiny.

177
00:11:59,067 --> 00:12:01,357
So, let's believe in him.

178
00:12:02,487 --> 00:12:03,697
Look at this, guys!

179
00:12:04,067 --> 00:12:06,827
Meat that's not rotten!

180
00:12:07,077 --> 00:12:10,617
I only see a man who wants to eat meat.

181
00:12:10,997 --> 00:12:13,707
It's all in your head, Mystras.

182
00:12:13,787 --> 00:12:15,077
It's all in your head.

183
00:12:20,957 --> 00:12:21,837
This time...

184
00:12:22,337 --> 00:12:23,337
They're gigantic!

185
00:12:24,297 --> 00:12:26,427
They're bigger than ever!

186
00:12:27,677 --> 00:12:30,217
So, what? We still have no way out.

187
00:12:30,847 --> 00:12:31,927
Mystras.

188
00:12:32,017 --> 00:12:33,057
I've been...

189
00:12:35,017 --> 00:12:38,227
waiting for this day to come.

190
00:12:39,437 --> 00:12:43,567
They're the carriers of our destiny!

191
00:12:47,817 --> 00:12:50,827
Good! That should be big enough.

192
00:12:51,617 --> 00:12:54,207
Come back with more precious stones!

193
00:12:54,287 --> 00:12:55,497
Yes, ma'am!

194
00:12:55,617 --> 00:12:58,667
I can't wait! Let's hurry!

195
00:12:59,167 --> 00:13:00,917
Since the meat's bigger,

196
00:13:01,337 --> 00:13:03,757
there's a lot more stones stuck to it.

197
00:13:09,677 --> 00:13:10,597
Hey there.

198
00:13:17,307 --> 00:13:19,107
I'm gonna borrow that cloth.

199
00:13:20,067 --> 00:13:22,107
-Good heavens.
-Please excuse us.

200
00:13:22,647 --> 00:13:25,777
We've been living in nature
for quite some time now.

201
00:13:26,857 --> 00:13:29,657
So, this was why you made us

202
00:13:30,077 --> 00:13:31,657
carve out the meat.

203
00:13:33,287 --> 00:13:34,787
What's this about?

204
00:13:35,247 --> 00:13:38,577
They drop meat into the bottom
of the snake-infested valley

205
00:13:38,957 --> 00:13:41,037
and make the birds pick up
precious stones.

206
00:13:42,167 --> 00:13:45,917
But we started to eat all of that meat.

207
00:13:46,627 --> 00:13:48,547
So, then, they started to think

208
00:13:49,257 --> 00:13:51,807
that a carnivore wandered
into the bottom of the valley

209
00:13:51,887 --> 00:13:54,137
and kept eating all of the meat.

210
00:13:55,017 --> 00:13:58,847
So, they decided to use
massive-sized pieces of meat

211
00:13:59,267 --> 00:14:01,937
that wouldn't get eaten
before the birds came to retrieve them.

212
00:14:03,527 --> 00:14:06,107
Yup. That's exactly what happened.

213
00:14:07,197 --> 00:14:09,907
I wondered why
I didn't see any men in the city.

214
00:14:10,237 --> 00:14:12,487
But they were forced to work here.

215
00:14:13,367 --> 00:14:15,327
Is it possible...

216
00:14:15,407 --> 00:14:17,867
that you're all treated unfairly
by women?

217
00:14:18,207 --> 00:14:19,207
Unfairly?

218
00:14:20,077 --> 00:14:21,957
Oh, of course not!

219
00:14:22,537 --> 00:14:24,457
We're just homemakers.

220
00:14:25,047 --> 00:14:28,627
Only women are allowed to handle animals
in this country.

221
00:14:28,927 --> 00:14:31,717
Women are the ones in charge of labor.

222
00:14:31,967 --> 00:14:36,017
Yes! Instead, men take on the housework
and protect the home.

223
00:14:36,097 --> 00:14:38,387
We take up side jobs like these, too.

224
00:14:38,477 --> 00:14:43,017
Women are busy bees,
working so hard every day.

225
00:14:43,477 --> 00:14:45,227
I totally agree.

226
00:14:46,437 --> 00:14:50,197
The roles of women and men are
completely switched in Artemyra society.

227
00:14:50,567 --> 00:14:53,527
I don't understand it at all.

228
00:14:54,117 --> 00:14:55,577
Let's get to work now.

229
00:14:55,657 --> 00:14:58,327
Looks like they're having
a lot of fun though.

230
00:14:58,407 --> 00:14:59,457
All right!

231
00:15:00,417 --> 00:15:03,127
Sinbad, the world is a vast place.

232
00:15:03,627 --> 00:15:04,877
Indeed.

233
00:15:05,877 --> 00:15:08,967
Now, shall we report to the queen

234
00:15:09,047 --> 00:15:11,887
and show her that we survived?

235
00:15:15,717 --> 00:15:17,767
That's all
for today's governmental affairs.

236
00:15:18,057 --> 00:15:20,847
Have a good night, Your Grace, Mira.

237
00:15:23,897 --> 00:15:27,227
How beautiful is this Metal Vessel
that houses the Djinn?

238
00:15:28,227 --> 00:15:31,947
It's a pity I can't demonstrate its power
since it belongs to another.

239
00:15:32,487 --> 00:15:35,987
But nothing else adorns me better.

240
00:15:36,077 --> 00:15:37,117
Adorns you?

241
00:15:37,487 --> 00:15:38,577
You're wrong.

242
00:15:38,657 --> 00:15:42,617
Your own beauty overpowers
everything around you.

243
00:15:43,377 --> 00:15:44,997
Sinbad?!

244
00:15:45,287 --> 00:15:47,417
I've returned
from the Valley of the Dead...

245
00:15:50,087 --> 00:15:51,417
to see you.

246
00:15:53,337 --> 00:15:56,007
-I wanted to see you.
-Wait.

247
00:15:58,847 --> 00:16:01,137
Yes, I needed to see you.

248
00:16:01,937 --> 00:16:04,347
Because you had my Metal Vessel.

249
00:16:05,267 --> 00:16:08,897
You're so cautious that you use dolls
to take your place in meetings.

250
00:16:09,527 --> 00:16:11,647
I knew that you would keep
the Metal Vessel

251
00:16:11,737 --> 00:16:14,277
where you can keep your eye on it
at all times.

252
00:16:15,407 --> 00:16:18,537
Your Excellency, is something the matter?

253
00:16:19,327 --> 00:16:22,747
Unforgivable.
I'll never forgive you for this, Sinbad.

254
00:16:23,747 --> 00:16:25,207
I'm going to...

255
00:16:25,287 --> 00:16:28,377
make you regret
how you insulted the queen,

256
00:16:28,457 --> 00:16:29,917
Mira Dianus Artemina.

257
00:16:31,297 --> 00:16:33,967
I'll never let a man get away
with such disrespect.

258
00:16:35,427 --> 00:16:37,097
My servant of sternness and fascination.

259
00:16:37,797 --> 00:16:38,967
Take shelter within me.

260
00:16:39,507 --> 00:16:42,227
Transform my whole body
into that of a great magus.

261
00:16:44,557 --> 00:16:45,477
Cerberus!

262
00:16:47,767 --> 00:16:50,527
Let me show you my powers.

263
00:16:53,067 --> 00:16:55,777
Do you think Sinbad is gonna be okay?

264
00:16:55,857 --> 00:16:58,577
Well, he's reckless as always.

265
00:16:59,157 --> 00:17:01,787
But we must save Hinahoho
as soon as possible.

266
00:17:02,157 --> 00:17:03,117
Ja'far!

267
00:17:04,247 --> 00:17:05,117
Look!

268
00:17:11,377 --> 00:17:12,547
Bararaq!

269
00:17:13,417 --> 00:17:14,377
Bararaq!

270
00:17:17,007 --> 00:17:20,387
Sinbad and the queen are fighting
with Djinn Equips?

271
00:17:20,467 --> 00:17:23,807
The queen's going to use
a lightning Djinn like Baal?

272
00:17:24,927 --> 00:17:27,977
Our lightning might cancel
each other out.

273
00:17:28,607 --> 00:17:30,767
I won't even feel your attacks.

274
00:17:31,647 --> 00:17:33,487
Then may I show you...

275
00:17:35,357 --> 00:17:37,857
the power of the other Djinn?

276
00:17:39,067 --> 00:17:43,117
As I captured several Dungeons
and subdued various Djinns,

277
00:17:43,787 --> 00:17:47,367
I'm able to switch Djinn Equips
and exercise their power.

278
00:17:48,577 --> 00:17:50,497
My servant of deception and confidence.

279
00:17:51,457 --> 00:17:54,007
Transform my whole body
into that of a great magus.

280
00:17:55,167 --> 00:17:57,047
Djinn Equip Valefor!

281
00:17:59,007 --> 00:18:00,347
Another Djinn Equip?

282
00:18:01,007 --> 00:18:03,927
Do you think that trick will work on me?

283
00:18:08,557 --> 00:18:09,937
What are you waiting for?

284
00:18:10,557 --> 00:18:11,767
If you won't attack...

285
00:18:12,357 --> 00:18:13,647
then I will!

286
00:18:18,657 --> 00:18:20,777
What, is that all you've got?

287
00:18:22,237 --> 00:18:23,827
Garufor Zairu!

288
00:18:24,287 --> 00:18:25,327
GARUFOR ZAIRU

289
00:18:29,327 --> 00:18:30,457
A direct hit!

290
00:18:30,957 --> 00:18:31,787
No.

291
00:18:32,587 --> 00:18:33,707
She's unharmed.

292
00:18:34,207 --> 00:18:35,667
Don't make me laugh.

293
00:18:35,957 --> 00:18:38,967
This is the "power"
of a multiple Dungeon Capturer?

294
00:18:40,137 --> 00:18:42,387
Cerberus is a three-headed Djinn.

295
00:18:42,967 --> 00:18:46,137
One governs ice
and the other governs lightning.

296
00:18:46,977 --> 00:18:49,937
And I, the main body, governs fire.

297
00:18:50,557 --> 00:18:53,647
I subdued the ultimate Djinn
that houses three different elements.

298
00:18:54,107 --> 00:18:56,227
I don't need to switch Djinn Equips.

299
00:18:56,987 --> 00:19:01,317
Possessing only two elements,
you cannot defeat me!

300
00:19:01,867 --> 00:19:04,327
I can't believe that such Djinn exists!

301
00:19:04,907 --> 00:19:06,287
There's no way you can win.

302
00:19:06,867 --> 00:19:08,827
At this rate, Sinbad's gonna...

303
00:19:09,657 --> 00:19:12,077
No, let's have faith in him.

304
00:19:12,877 --> 00:19:15,457
Sin must have a plan.

305
00:19:18,297 --> 00:19:19,797
I'll knock you down to the ground!

306
00:19:21,257 --> 00:19:22,887
Cerbero Hadisa!

307
00:19:22,967 --> 00:19:24,007
CERBERO HADISA

308
00:19:25,177 --> 00:19:26,307
Sinbad!

309
00:19:30,557 --> 00:19:32,017
Well, that was close.

310
00:19:32,767 --> 00:19:34,647
But this is the end!

311
00:19:40,027 --> 00:19:42,197
Cerbero Jairu Ranquesa!

312
00:19:42,277 --> 00:19:43,987
CERBERO JAIRU RANQUESA

313
00:19:48,157 --> 00:19:49,577
Sinbad...

314
00:19:52,167 --> 00:19:53,497
How easy.

315
00:19:53,917 --> 00:19:57,837
Guess you were just like
all the other men,

316
00:19:57,917 --> 00:19:59,377
Sinbad.

317
00:20:01,297 --> 00:20:04,927
Your Excellency, I'm not dead yet.

318
00:20:06,847 --> 00:20:09,217
You... How are you here?

319
00:20:10,227 --> 00:20:12,227
How did he pull this off from that stance?

320
00:20:13,187 --> 00:20:16,727
It's working. Valefor's true powers.

321
00:20:17,227 --> 00:20:18,397
True powers?

322
00:20:18,727 --> 00:20:19,647
Yes.

323
00:20:19,727 --> 00:20:22,357
Valefor manipulates ice and snow,

324
00:20:22,697 --> 00:20:25,367
but that's only part of his true power.

325
00:20:26,027 --> 00:20:28,867
You insolent bastard,
running is all you can do?

326
00:20:29,327 --> 00:20:32,157
But you won't be able to escape this.

327
00:20:33,367 --> 00:20:35,787
Fire, lightning and ice.

328
00:20:36,167 --> 00:20:40,257
The ultimate annihilation magic
that combines all three elements.

329
00:20:40,837 --> 00:20:42,917
I'll turn you into ash!

330
00:20:44,297 --> 00:20:47,427
Maximum magic!
Cerbero Kalb Volquesa!

331
00:20:47,507 --> 00:20:48,637
CERBERO KALB VOLQUESA

332
00:20:51,467 --> 00:20:52,347
Impossible!

333
00:20:52,677 --> 00:20:54,767
You cannot do that, Your Excellency.

334
00:20:55,347 --> 00:20:58,397
You'll end up harming the country
that it's your duty to protect.

335
00:20:59,227 --> 00:21:02,607
How is he able to come up behind me?

336
00:21:03,067 --> 00:21:06,357
I never took my eyes off him.

337
00:21:06,987 --> 00:21:11,237
Bastard!
I refuse to be dictated to by a man!

338
00:21:12,407 --> 00:21:13,747
I'm over here.

339
00:21:14,407 --> 00:21:17,997
What's happening?
My attacks are completely wasted.

340
00:21:20,707 --> 00:21:25,167
It's like fighting someone...
from another dimension.

341
00:21:26,547 --> 00:21:28,757
-The queen's moves...
-Yes.

342
00:21:29,217 --> 00:21:31,387
Valefor's ability is "stagnation."

343
00:21:32,097 --> 00:21:37,437
His power to limit the target's movement
is the true ability of that Djinn Equip.

344
00:21:38,147 --> 00:21:39,807
The hail earlier

345
00:21:39,897 --> 00:21:42,527
was created by solidifying water drops

346
00:21:42,607 --> 00:21:44,737
floating in the air.

347
00:21:45,397 --> 00:21:49,697
He then applied the stagnation power
to the queen herself.

348
00:21:50,197 --> 00:21:53,367
It weakened the queen quite a bit.

349
00:21:53,827 --> 00:21:56,867
But she still has no idea...

350
00:22:02,667 --> 00:22:08,007
This can't be! This is the first time
in my life a man has...

351
00:22:08,887 --> 00:22:11,547
I prefer not to treat women this way.

352
00:22:14,267 --> 00:22:16,807
Garufor Kirestal!

353
00:22:19,767 --> 00:22:23,607
The first man to ever... defeat me.

